  "issue": 2511,
  "purpose": "Acceptance inputs for the Rust entry builder (#1282 D2): a save the builder must root byte-identically, the schema-20 key vocabulary it must parse, and the measurement that lets it read RNG stream state out of the save instead of deriving it from a per-build seeding scheme. No captured save or .mcr bytes appear here; the one save is synthetic and the census carries key names and counts only.",
  "refusal_cases": {
    "card_owner_provenance": "SerializableCard has no Owner field (IL, v0.111.0). For a Colorless or off-character card whose generation pool depends on the owner, the save cannot answer and the builder refuses by name. This is the class Python refuses 79 times; whether Rust must refuse it too is a per-mechanic question the slice answers one generator at a time, not an assumption.",
    "missing_map_point_history": "current_act_index >= 1 with no map_point_history. The global node index feeds total_floor and therefore the per-fight Encounter stream; 65 of 3092 schema-20 saves omit the key, which is harmless at act 0 and fatal after it.",
    "multiplayer_save": "players.len() != 1. Mirrors relay_parser.require_single_player; every schema-20 save in the corpus is single-player, so this is unexercised and must refuse rather than select players[0].",
    "note": "Names the Rust builder must be able to emit. Each is a fact the schema-20 save either genuinely lacks or records ambiguously; I5 says refuse by name rather than guess. The digest-parity corpus acceptance is what fixes the full list \u2014 these are the ones derivable statically from the save-writer IL and the corpus census.",
    "saved_property_group_unhandled": "SavedProperties defines seven groups (ints, bools, strings, intArrays, modelIds, cards, cardArrays). Only five appear in the corpus (ints, bools, strings, cards, model_ids); intArrays and cardArrays must parse and refuse-by-name rather than be dropped, because Fur Coat's coordinate latch is an intArray.",
    "unknown_node_type": "The visited coord is not in the current act's saved_map, or its type is 'unknown' (the ? node, 35547 points in the corpus). The encounter then comes from the NEXT save's pre_finished_room, which this input does not carry \u2014 the census's no_encounter class (17 fights).",
    "unsupported_save_schema": "schema_version != 20. The corpus holds 16/18/19 saves; the SerializableRunV{n}To V{n+1} migration chain is the authority for what changed, and nothing below 20 is admitted."
  },
